  },
  "classification": "Product retry-cancellation race, exposed by a test ordering assumption",
  "cause": [
    "The post-kill barrier resolved on any effect read containing only retained kill boundaries. The automatic one-second retry itself could satisfy it, moving the baseline past the retry and hiding the extra read.",
    "An explicit non-fresh kick drained the kill and failed send, but the controller cancelled its pending DeliveryWake only for fresh admissions. The old one-second timer remained armed and later ran a redundant queue pass."
  ],
  "fix": [
    "Use the journal's terminal kill and send receipts as the completion condition; do not issue a second kick before starting the existing 1,100 ms quietness window.",
    "Cancel the owned delayed DeliveryWake on every explicit queue kick, which supersedes the stale retry while preserving the fresh-admission distinction for queue retry admission."
  ],
  "preserved": {
    "existingAssertions": "All operation, host, recovery and effectBatch quietness assertions retained",
